WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:06.819
A Song of Ice and Fire is a huge, complicated
story, with literally thousands of characters

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:11.280
– twenty-two of whom are named Jon – so
it’s fair enough that the show, Game of

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.679
Thrones, had to simplify things a bit by cutting
and combining many characters.

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:19.619
It’s a shame though, because many of even
the minor characters have heaps of really

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:24.910
cool backstories, and connections, and layers
to them, that add a lot to the series.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.759
A good example is Thoros of Myr.

00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:31.769
We know him in the show as a member of the
“brotherhood without banners”, the outlaw

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:35.980
group who capture Arya, Gendry and Hot Pie
in Season 3.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:41.310
The leader of the brotherhood, Beric Dondarrion,
is killed by the Hound, but then Thoros resurrects

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:46.190
Beric using the power of the Red God, R’hllor
– which may forshadow a certain other red

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.560
priest resurrecting a certain Jon Snow, not
to name any names, but anyway, that’s basically

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.550
Thoros’ role in the show so far.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.800
But in the books, there’s more to his story.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.140
Thoros was born in the city of Myr.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.600
He was the youngest of eight children, so
his father gave him to a temple of R’hllor,

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.829
where Thoros was trained to be a red priest.

00:01:06.829 --> 00:01:10.700
He “prayed the prayers and … spoke the
spells”, and did sometimes see visions in

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.700
flames, but he wasn’t much of a believer,
being more interested in food and women.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.221
Eventually he was sent to Westeros to convert
King Aerys Targaryen to the faith of the Red

00:01:20.221 --> 00:01:21.221
God.

00:01:21.221 --> 00:01:25.390
The temple figured that since Mad Aerys infamously
“loved fire”, he might like the Lord of

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.789
Light, but Thoros failed to convert Aerys.

00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:32.950
When Aerys was overthrown, Thoros became bros
with the new king, Robert Baratheon.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:37.460
“They were pease in a pod … both gluttons
and sots” – who loved eating and drinking

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:42.940
and whoring and fighting . Thoros would fight
in tourneys with his sword alight with wildfire

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:47.529
. And he fought in the Greyjoy Rebellion,
“setting ironmen afire with every slash”

00:01:47.529 --> 00:01:51.670
of his “flaming sword” . So he sounds
like quite the warrior, but in the same way

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:58.759
that Bobby B is a pretty shitty king, Thoros
is a pretty shitty priest . Tywin calls him

00:01:58.759 --> 00:02:03.610
a “fat jape” , and Gendry’s master Tobho
– who sells Thoros the swords he sets afire

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:08.940
– calls him “a fraud”, and “as bad
a priest as there ever was” . Thoros apparently

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:14.740
gives up trying to convert anyone, and doesn’t
seem to even believe in R’hllor anymore.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:18.800
But all that changes in the War of the Five
Kings.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:24.640
In Book 1, the Mountain, Gregor Clegane, starts
brutally raiding in the riverlands . So Ned

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:29.150
Stark, acting on the behalf of King Robert,
orders a group of men to go stop him.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.820
The group is led by Lord Beric Dondarrion,
and includes about a hundred men, including

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.000
Thoros.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.760
So the men go after the Mountain, but at the
Mummer’s Ford, they’re ambushed – the

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.540
whole thing was a trap designed by Tywin Lannister
to get Ned – the only reason it didn’t

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:47.480
work was ‘cause Ned couldn’t come because
Jaime injured his leg . So anyway, the group

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.180
is smashed by the Mountain’s men.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:54.010
Some of them manage to escape, and regroup,
but Beric is mortally wounded, with a lance

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:55.220
run through his chest.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:03:00.750
Thoros, distraught over his dying friend,
performs a “death rite” of the red priests,

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:04.790
called the “last kiss”, breathing fire
into Beric’s body.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:10.980
To Thoros’ shock, the dead man shudders,
his eyes come open, and Beric is brought back

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.590
to life .
This causes a religious reawakening for Thoros,

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:19.170
he says “The Lord of Light has woken in
[his] heart” .

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:23.569
As the remnants of Beric’s men regroup,
Thoros converts them to his rediscovered faith

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:29.191
, binding them together as a holy brotherhood,
sworn to serve their realm, their god, and

00:03:29.191 --> 00:03:33.820
each other . Even after King Robert dies,
the brotherhood fights on in his name, protecting

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:38.910
the common people from the ravages of raiders
like Gregor . They fight a guerrilla war against

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:42.990
the Lannisters in the riverlands, striking
suddenly , then “vanishing back into the

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:47.410
woods” . Thoros fights in these battles
with his flaming sword, he sees visions in

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:52.810
his flames of the future, present and past
, and he resurrects Beric five more times

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.090
as he keeps dying in his fights.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:59.810
Thoros is convinced that he’s an “instrument”
of “God” , he’s finally doing something

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:02.400
with his life that he believes in.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.940
And it changes him.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:08.100
When Arya first sees Thoros with the brotherhood,
she hardly believes it’s him.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:13.210
She “remember[s] the red priest as fat,
with a smooth face and a shiny bald head”.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:17.459
But now Thoros “ha[s] a droopy face and
a full head of shaggy grey hair”.

00:04:17.459 --> 00:04:22.060
Thoros says that a year in the wild has melted
the flesh off him, that “[he is] less than

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:28.160
[he] was, but more” . This change in appearance
mirrors the change in his character from a

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:33.090
“glutton” and a “sot”, a fat joke
of a priest, to a man filled with righteous

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.660
purpose and faith.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.210
But his story doesn’t end there.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:42.120
] In the last Brienne chapter of Feast, we
hear that Beric Dondarrion has died a final

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:49.210
time, giving his “flame of life” to the
dead Catelyn Stark, who rises as Lady Stoneheart

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:54.690
. Stoneheart is totally different to what
Catelyn was like alive, she’s vengeful,

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:59.071
hateful , completely without mercy , and as
the new leader of the “brotherhood”, she

00:04:59.071 --> 00:05:04.760
begins a brutal campaign killing everyone
who’s in any way connected to the Red Wedding,

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:09.740
even people who really weren’t responsible,
like Petyr and Merrett Frey , she evens hangs

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:13.570
Podrick – though Pod is apparently still
alive , so don’t worry – but the point

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:18.841
is that under Stoneheart, the brotherhood
does some fucked up stuff . Under Beric, they

00:05:18.841 --> 00:05:22.840
would always give their captives a trial,
they “won’t kill a man unless something’s

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:28.500
proved against him” , but Stoneheart will
hang anyone who she deems guilty . Thoros

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:33.770
loses his belief that what they’re doing
is just , he loses his belief in himself,

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:38.740
calling himself a “pink pretender”, “a
bad priest and a worse wizard” . He sees

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:44.169
the brotherhood, his brotherhood, deteriorate
from something noble and righteous and holy

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:51.389
to something crueller and darker . He says
that “War makes monsters of us all”.

00:05:51.389 --> 00:05:55.430
So… where can Thoros go from here?

00:05:55.430 --> 00:06:00.060
Maybe Thoros could just leave, kinda like
the Hound did – the popular Gravedigger

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:05.560
theory suggests that Sandor Clegane is not
dead, but living a life of peace and atonement

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.949
as a monk on the Quiet Isle.

00:06:07.949 --> 00:06:12.610
Maybe Thoros could do something similar, go
back to a red temple in Essos and meditate

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:14.630
on his God and his place in the world.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:18.889
Alternatively, he could try to finish what
he started, maybe try to put the brotherhood

00:06:18.889 --> 00:06:22.790
back on a righteous path by killing Lady Stoneheart.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:28.370
Thoros after all is a fire priest with a flaming
sword, and the undead in this story generally

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.270
are vulnerable to fire.

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:34.540
Trying to kill Stoneheart could risk Thoros’
life, but he might think it’s worth the

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:40.210
sacrifice – Thoros tells Brienne that “it
does not matter how a man begins, but only

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.680
how he ends”.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:47.120
Sacrificing himself to kill Stoneheart could
make a great ending for Thoros, a dramatic

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:51.510
act of selflessness by a formerly selfish
man.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:56.449
So it could go a bunch of ways, but the point
is that Thoros is a really fascinating character,

00:06:56.449 --> 00:07:01.949
someone who transforms from a drunken warrior,
to a righteous priest, to a man again filled

00:07:01.949 --> 00:07:04.229
with doubts about what he’s become.

00:07:04.229 --> 00:07:08.040
It’ll be great to see how his story ends
in the books – he might even turn up again

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:11.680
in the show, we’ll have to wait and see,
it’s not clear if the show will include

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.800
the whole Stoneheart thing.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:18.310
By the way, this artwork of Stoneheart was
created by Ertaç Altınöz, you might like

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.390
to check out his DeviantArt for more.

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:22.460
